458
00:56:08.326 --> 00:56:13.747
Really? We've got an extra ticket
for the St. John's game. Want to come?

459
00:56:15.291 --> 00:56:16.834
Yes.

460
00:56:17.043 --> 00:56:20.587
You can double -date
with me and Darryl

461
00:56:46.489 --> 00:56:48.782
In his face! In his face!

462
00:56:48.992 --> 00:56:51.744
Yes! In the face!

463
00:56:55.248 --> 00:56:58.334
Why don't you take off your jacket,
Akeem?

464
00:56:58.543 --> 00:57:02.046
"Put it in the face," right? I like this.

465
00:57:03.089 --> 00:57:06.300
- Isn't that better?
- Yes, thank you very much.

466
00:57:14.017 --> 00:57:17.686
Wearing clothes must be
a new experience for you.

467
00:57:17.896 --> 00:57:21.940
- Are you able to follow the game?
- Oh, yes!

468
00:57:22.150 --> 00:57:25.402
I'm following the game quite well.

469
00:57:27.238 --> 00:57:31.200
What kind of games do you play
in Africa? Chase the monkey?

470
00:57:32.619 --> 00:57:35.996
No, we play football.
I believe you call it soccer.

471
00:57:36.206 --> 00:57:38.082
Yeah, right. Soccer.

472
00:57:38.291 --> 00:57:44.213
That's a real cute sport. Especially the
way you bounce the ball off your heads.

473
00:57:44.422 --> 00:57:48.384
I don't like any sport
where you don't use your hands.

474
00:57:49.552 --> 00:57:51.970
Yes! Yes!

475
00:57:52.180 --> 00:57:56.100
What are you doing?
It's just the half-time?

476
00:57:57.143 --> 00:58:01.230
This is my favourite part of the game.
Will you excuse me for a moment?

477
00:58:01.439 --> 00:58:05.025
Excuse me. I'll be back in a minute.

478
00:58:19.499 --> 00:58:22.835
Oh, my goodness!
Oh, my goodness, it is you!

479
00:58:23.920 --> 00:58:26.255
I cannot believe it.

480
00:58:29.300 --> 00:58:33.220
- Greetings, your Highness.
- Please, stop bowing.

481
00:58:33.430 --> 00:58:37.599
- I am a loyal citizen of Zamunda.
- You will spill your beverages.

482
00:58:38.727 --> 00:58:41.895
This is the greatest day of my life.

483
00:58:42.814 --> 00:58:46.859
It was very nice meeting you, too.
Excuse me.

484
00:58:50.447 --> 00:58:55.117
Please! Please, may I just have
my picture taken with you?

485
00:59:06.504 --> 00:59:12.092
I will cherish this experience
for the rest of my life.

486
00:59:18.058 --> 00:59:20.934
For the rest of my life.

487
00:59:23.396 --> 00:59:27.816
- Who was that?
- Just a man I met in the restroom.

488
00:59:35.492 --> 00:59:39.828
- Why don't you quit this job?
- Because I like it here.

489
00:59:40.038 --> 00:59:43.832
But you're my lady.
My lady doesn't have to work.

490
00:59:45.168 --> 00:59:48.712
I'll take care of you.
Get you anything you want.

491
00:59:49.964 --> 00:59:52.883
- What can I get you?
- Nothing.

492
00:59:54.844 --> 00:59:57.971
I'll get you some ...  coffee.

493
00:59:59.349 --> 01:00:02.101
I'll be right back.

494
01:00:09.025 --> 01:00:12.027
Hey, Akeem. Did you have
a good time at the game?

495
01:00:12.237 --> 01:00:13.654
Yes, I did.

496
01:00:13.863 --> 01:00:17.449
I hope Darryl didn't offend you.
He can be pretty obnoxious.

497
01:00:17.659 --> 01:00:21.704
- He cannot help it.
- Sit down, take a break for a minute.

498
01:00:25.417 --> 01:00:27.876
You're an unusual guy.

499
01:00:28.086 --> 01:00:31.213
I've never seen anybody take
so much pride in mopping a floor.

500
01:00:31.423 --> 01:00:35.509
"He who would learn to fly
must first learn to stand and walk."

501
01:00:35.719 --> 01:00:40.597
"One cannot fly into flying."
That's not mine, that's Nietzsche's.

502
01:00:40.807 --> 01:00:44.643
That's what I mean. The guys
that work here don't quote Nietzsche.

503
01:00:49.774 --> 01:00:53.110
Everybody shut up and do what I say.

504
01:00:53.319 --> 01:00:57.823
Get the money out!
Stay cool, nobody gets hurt.

505
01:00:58.033 --> 01:01:00.492
Take the money out! All of it.

506
01:01:00.702 --> 01:01:03.787
Don't stall me, fat boy. Let's go.

507
01:01:03.997 --> 01:01:07.583
Come on! You're wasting my time.
Come on!

508
01:01:11.046 --> 01:01:14.048
Anybody move,
I'll blow your fucking head off.

509
01:01:14.257 --> 01:01:17.509
What are you looking at, buddy?

510
01:01:19.387 --> 01:01:23.057
Come on! Stop stalling.

511
01:01:25.560 --> 01:01:29.730
Come on. Don't stall me. All of it!

512
01:01:34.819 --> 01:01:38.614
- Come on!
- Excuse me for a moment.

513
01:01:44.829 --> 01:01:46.789
It would be wise for you
to put the weapon down.

514
01:01:46.998 --> 01:01:49.208
Who is this asshole?

515
01:01:50.835 --> 01:01:55.547
Please refrain from using any more
obscenities in front of these people.

516
01:01:55.757 --> 01:01:58.425
I've warned you.
I'll be forced to thrash you.

517
01:01:58.635 --> 01:02:00.636
Fuck you!

518
01:02:05.934 --> 01:02:09.561
Freeze,
you diseased rhinoceros' pizzle.

519
01:02:21.866 --> 01:02:26.578
Hey, fellas. I'm real proud of the job
you did in there today.

520
01:02:26.788 --> 01:02:29.331
We've been hit by that guy five times,

521
01:02:29.541 --> 01:02:34.503
but I don't think he's coming back,
thanks to my African connections.

522
01:02:36.256 --> 01:02:41.844
Leave Sunday night open.
I'm having a get-together at my house.

523
01:02:43.555 --> 01:02:45.681
You see?
He has accepted us as equals.

524
01:02:48.518 --> 01:02:53.313
OK, fellas. Give them a ticket, take their
keys and park the cars down the street.

525
01:02:53.523 --> 01:02:56.358
When you're finished, come inside
and help out in the kitchen.

526
01:02:56.568 --> 01:03:02.406
Akeem, I want to show you
the inside of McDowell's little castle.

527
01:03:07.203 --> 01:03:12.374
This here is my showplace.
It pretty much speaks for itself.

528
01:03:13.626 --> 01:03:20.257
When I grew up, nine of us lived
in a shack no bigger than this room.

529
01:03:20.967 --> 01:03:24.136
And look what I have today.

530
01:03:24.346 --> 01:03:27.598
I only wish Mrs McDowell
could have lived to see it.

531
01:03:27.807 --> 01:03:31.643
- You have a fine house, sir.
- Thank you.

532
01:03:31.853 --> 01:03:37.358
In 20 or 30 years, with hard work,
maybe you could have a place like this.

533
01:03:40.945 --> 01:03:43.530
- That would be something.
- Wouldn't it?

534
01:03:47.494 --> 01:03:51.121
This is where you're going
to be working tonight.

535
01:03:59.714 --> 01:04:04.510
- Ever open a champagne bottle?
- I have seen it done before.

536
01:04:04.719 --> 01:04:07.513
Make sure you keep all the glasses full.

537
01:04:07.722 --> 01:04:12.142
I'd better get dressed. Make yourself
comfortable 'til the guests arrive.

538
01:04:15.313 --> 01:04:20.984
I love the Lord. Do you understand
what I'm saying? I love the Lord.

539
01:04:21.194 --> 01:04:25.155
And if loving the Lord is wrong,
I don't want to be right.

540
01:04:25.365 --> 01:04:30.953
Hi, Mike. Good to see you. Enjoy, drink
up. Lots more where that came from.

541
01:04:31.204 --> 01:04:35.374
Hey, Randy! Good to see you.
Watch out for this guy.

542
01:04:35.583 --> 01:04:37.376
Big Ed, my man!

543
01:04:38.420 --> 01:04:42.840
You know, I can appreciate the way
you handled that dude with the gun.

544
01:04:43.466 --> 01:04:46.343
I would've helped you out, except ... 

545
01:04:46.553 --> 01:04:49.596
I had a cup of coffee in my hand.
You understand, right?

546
01:04:49.806 --> 01:04:55.519
I bet you learnt all that stuff
fighting lions and tigers and shit.

547
01:04:55.729 --> 01:04:59.356
Yes, where I'm from,
we have to be very aggressive.

548
01:04:59.566 --> 01:05:03.235
I'm all for that. Especially with women.

549
01:05:04.029 --> 01:05:06.822
They may not admit it ... 

550
01:05:07.032 --> 01:05:11.785
 ... but they all want
a man to take charge.

551
01:05:16.499 --> 01:05:19.585
Tell them what to do.

552
01:05:27.427 --> 01:05:29.636
That's one of the things
I want to talk to you ... 

553
01:05:29.846 --> 01:05:34.350
Darryl, your mother gets lovelier
every time I see her.

554
01:05:34.559 --> 01:05:39.521
- Cleo, I'd like to talk to you alone.
- Sure. Excuse us.

555
01:05:39.731 --> 01:05:43.025
- Mum, Dad, Grandma ... 
- Sure, son.

556
01:05:43.234 --> 01:05:47.571
I like the fries better at McDonald's,
but I'd never tell Mr McDowell that.

557
01:05:49.699 --> 01:05:52.701
Make sure everybody's glass
is kept full.

558
01:05:52.911 --> 01:05:56.663
We're about to make
a very special announcement.

559
01:06:01.211 --> 01:06:04.505
May I have
everyone's attention, please.

560
01:06:08.218 --> 01:06:13.555
Mr and Mrs Jenks, would you join me?
Mother Jenks, you come up here, too.

561
01:06:22.982 --> 01:06:26.443
I've just heard some news
that makes me a very happy man.

562
01:06:26.653 --> 01:06:28.195
Semmi, please ... 

563
01:06:30.740 --> 01:06:33.075
Champagne.

564
01:06:34.244 --> 01:06:37.162
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

565
01:06:37.372 --> 01:06:40.833
Okay, get going. Get out of here. Go on.

566
01:06:42.961 --> 01:06:48.716
As you know, Darryl and Lisa have
been going together for quite some time.

567
01:06:48.925 --> 01:06:54.096
I'm pleased to announce
that Darryl just popped the big question.

568
01:06:56.349 --> 01:06:59.643
And Lisa happily accepted.

569
01:07:06.943 --> 01:07:10.571
So as it turns out, this has become
an engagement party.

570
01:07:11.364 --> 01:07:14.950
Amen! Praise the Lord.

571
01:07:15.160 --> 01:07:19.329
- Married?
- To the bride and groom.

572
01:07:19.539 --> 01:07:21.540
To the bride and groom!

573
01:07:21.750 --> 01:07:23.876
To the bride and groom.

574
01:07:31.384 --> 01:07:35.554
I want you and that young man
to tie that knot. I'll pray for you.

575
01:07:35.764 --> 01:07:38.724
And I want you to hold on
to God's unchanging hand.

576
01:07:38.933 --> 01:07:42.603
'Cause he helped Joshua
fight the battle of Jericho.

577
01:07:43.855 --> 01:07:46.732
And he helped Daniel
get out of the lion's den.

578
01:07:46.941 --> 01:07:51.111
He helped Gilligan get off the island.
Lord!

579
01:07:51.321 --> 01:07:54.365
I want to talk to you, now!

580
01:08:04.459 --> 01:08:09.505
The next time you and my father
plan my life, let me in on it.

581
01:08:09.714 --> 01:08:12.091
- It's not like ... 
- Don't touch me!

582
01:08:12.300 --> 01:08:15.594
But baby, it's our engagement party.

583
01:08:26.815 --> 01:08:28.774
Thanks.

584
01:08:35.949 --> 01:08:41.495
- Would you like some champagne?
- No, I don't feel like celebrating.

585
01:08:43.998 --> 01:08:48.585
Wait. Sit down and keep me company.

586
01:08:57.470 --> 01:09:01.140
If you're going to hang out with me,
you've got to loosen up.

587
01:09:01.349 --> 01:09:04.184
I can be loose. See?

588
01:09:05.520 --> 01:09:07.521
Much better.

589
01:09:09.190 --> 01:09:12.151
- Are you all right?
- I'm fine.

590
01:09:12.360 --> 01:09:17.197
But I won't be pressured into marriage,
not by Darryl, my father or anybody.

591
01:09:18.158 --> 01:09:21.702
I understand.
In my country they arrange marriages,

592
01:09:21.911 --> 01:09:24.621
but no one should marry
out of obligation.

593
01:09:24.831 --> 01:09:30.461
You're right. How could I even have
considered marrying a guy like Darryl

594
01:09:30.670 --> 01:09:36.300
- I wondered the same thing.
- He made me so furious back there.

595
01:09:36.509 --> 01:09:41.513
- Do you think I overreacted?
- The first reaction is often correct.

596
01:09:43.183 --> 01:09:47.686
You're very easy to talk to.
I feel like I could tell you anything.

597
01:09:53.443 --> 01:09:58.113
Hey, Akeem. We need
some more champagne over here.

598
01:09:59.908 --> 01:10:03.118
I almost forgot that I was here
in a domestic capacity.

599
01:10:03.328 --> 01:10:07.706
Thanks for listening to me, Akeem.
I really appreciate it.

600
01:10:07.916 --> 01:10:11.085
Anytime, Lisa McDowell.

601
01:10:15.924 --> 01:10:18.509
Hey! Be careful

602
01:10:19.761 --> 01:10:23.097
I think my sister likes you.

603
01:10:30.438 --> 01:10:32.439
Semmi!

604
01:10:35.068 --> 01:10:37.111
Semmi.

605
01:10:41.825 --> 01:10:48.163
- Come, you're going to be late for work.
- So what if I am?

606
01:10:48.373 --> 01:10:53.168
We cannot anger Mr McDowell.
Things are going so well with Lisa.

607
01:10:53.378 --> 01:10:57.256
I do not care.
I'm not going to work today.

608
01:10:57.507 --> 01:11:00.592
Yes, you are going to work today.

609
01:11:01.636 --> 01:11:04.179
I'm sick of living like a peasant.
Look at this filth.

610
01:11:04.389 --> 01:11:08.851
Do you want to live better? Fine.
Fix this place up.

611
01:11:09.060 --> 01:11:11.729
But you are going to work today!

612
01:11:21.614 --> 01:11:23.782
- Hello!
- Hi!

613
01:11:23.992 --> 01:11:27.703
I started on clean-up just like you guys,
but now ... 

614
01:11:27.912 --> 01:11:33.083
See, I'm washing lettuce.
Soon, I'll be on fries. Then the grill.

615
01:11:33.918 --> 01:11:36.962
In a year or two,
I'll make assistant manager

616
01:11:37.172 --> 01:11:40.466
and that's where the big bucks
start rolling in.

617
01:11:40.675 --> 01:11:43.510
Just two years, huh?

618
01:11:47.223 --> 01:11:52.603
Maybe I've stayed with him
because everyone expected me to.

619
01:11:52.812 --> 01:11:56.732
- You must be tired of my problems.
- No, not at all.

620
01:11:58.026 --> 01:12:00.778
I feel like I owe you a favour.

621
01:12:00.987 --> 01:12:05.908
Come to my house and I'll fix
you dinner. Patrice will be there.

622
01:12:06.117 --> 01:12:10.496
Let's go to my house.
I'd like to cook for you.

623
01:12:10.705 --> 01:12:14.333
- You cook?
- I dabble a little, yes.

624
01:12:14.542 --> 01:12:17.461
Great! Tell you what,
I'll buy the groceries.

625
01:12:17.671 --> 01:12:23.008
Fine. But I have to warn you.
My home is very poor.

626
01:12:23.218 --> 01:12:27.513
I don't care about that.
I'd love to see where you live.

627
01:12:41.069 --> 01:12:44.071
Welcome to my humble abode.

628
01:12:52.789 --> 01:12:56.583
- What's wrong?
- Nothing's wrong.

629
01:12:56.793 --> 01:13:01.088
Everything's fine.
Excuse me for a moment, please.

630
01:13:05.343 --> 01:13:08.971
- What have you done?
- You told me to fix up the place.

631
01:13:10.932 --> 01:13:14.810
I should kill you!
I'm supposed to be a poor man.

632
01:13:15.020 --> 01:13:18.022
Akeem? Akeem.

633
01:13:20.859 --> 01:13:23.068
- Is everything all right?
- Everything is fine.

634
01:13:23.278 --> 01:13:26.030
Excuse me, I have to tidy up.

635
01:13:42.213 --> 01:13:44.882
What are you doing?

636
01:13:47.010 --> 01:13:50.596
For God's sake,
do not take my pocket money.

637
01:13:55.268 --> 01:13:58.437
If you have no more money,
you can cause no more mischief.

638
01:13:58.646 --> 01:14:01.398
You are being unreasonable.

639
01:14:01.608 --> 01:14:07.529
If you have ruined my chances
with Lisa, I will never forgive you.

640
01:14:10.867 --> 01:14:13.369
- I'm very sorry.
- Can we go in now?

641
01:14:13.578 --> 01:14:16.622
- No, we cannot.
- Why not?

642
01:14:16.831 --> 01:14:20.250
There's a big rat inside.

643
01:14:20.460 --> 01:14:23.170
I think there is no rat.

644
01:14:23.380 --> 01:14:28.842
You're so ashamed of your apartment
you can't even let me see it.

645
01:14:29.052 --> 01:14:32.388
Once again, you have judged correctly.

646
01:14:32.597 --> 01:14:37.393
- If it bothers you, we can go out to eat.
- That would be much better.

647
01:15:03.211 --> 01:15:05.879
Excuse me for a moment, please.

648
01:15:15.432 --> 01:15:20.185
- What did you give him?
- I just gave him some pocket change.

649
01:15:34.868 --> 01:15:38.078
- Randolph ... 
- Leave me alone, Mortimer.

650
01:15:38.288 --> 01:15:41.248
Randolph! Randolph!

651
01:15:42.959 --> 01:15:47.004
- I'm still not talking to you.
- Look!

652
01:15:53.970 --> 01:15:57.348
Mortimer, we're back.

653
01:15:57.557 --> 01:16:00.267
Yeah!

654
01:16:00.977 --> 01:16:03.354
To America!

655
01:16:07.525 --> 01:16:09.651
Why did you come here?

656
01:16:09.861 --> 01:16:13.364
- To find something special
- it's a long way to travel

657
01:16:13.573 --> 01:16:18.327
No journey is too great,
when one finds what he seeks.

658
01:16:18.536 --> 01:16:22.956
- Does everyone in Africa talk like you?
- Why, do you not like it?

659
01:16:23.166 --> 01:16:28.879
I love it. It's nice to be with a man
who knows how to express himself.

660
01:16:29.923 --> 01:16:31.840
- Thank you!
- Thank you very much!

661
01:16:32.050 --> 01:16:34.468
Let's have lunch.

662
01:16:37.806 --> 01:16:41.141
You have the most amazing effect
on people.

663
01:16:41.351 --> 01:16:46.313
- No, I don'.
- Take the guy at the basketball game.

664
01:16:46.523 --> 01:16:49.149
People love you.

665
01:16:50.110 --> 01:16:54.780
I bet where you're from,
women throw themselves at your feet.

666
01:16:54.989 --> 01:17:00.494
- Why do you say that?
- You have an inner glow.

667
01:17:00.704 --> 01:17:04.832
You're above anything petty.
It's almost regal

668
01:17:08.837 --> 01:17:15.509
- What did you do back home?
- I was ...  in the family business.

669
01:17:16.386 --> 01:17:20.264
- What's that?
- Goat herding.

670
01:17:21.266 --> 01:17:24.351
Yes, yes. Does it surprise you?

671
01:17:24.561 --> 01:17:27.730
No, it's just that you seem so educated.

672
01:17:27.939 --> 01:17:33.110
The life of a goat herder is easy,
the goats take care of themselves.

673
01:17:33.319 --> 01:17:37.448
Which leaves a man
with a great deal of time to read.

674
01:17:40.285 --> 01:17:43.996
- Please, let me.
- No, I should pay.

675
01:17:44.205 --> 01:17:47.791
Akeem, I wish you'd stop
worrying about being poor.

676
01:17:48.001 --> 01:17:51.795
If I wanted a wealthy guy,
I'd be with Darryl

677
01:17:52.005 --> 01:17:54.340
Not you.

678
01:17:59.512 --> 01:18:03.557
- Would you like to dance?
- Yes.

679
01:18:31.795 --> 01:18:34.755
What about Patrice?

680
01:18:34.964 --> 01:18:38.467
I'm not interested in Patrice.

681
01:18:39.844 --> 01:18:42.471
What about Darryl

682
01:18:42.681 --> 01:18:46.058
I'm not interested in Darryl, either.

683
01:19:11.710 --> 01:19:16.046
- Do you actually want to send this?
- Why? What is wrong?

684
01:19:16.256 --> 01:19:17.881
Read it to me.

685
01:19:18.091 --> 01:19:23.804
"To his Majesty King Jaffe Joffer,
the Royal Palace, Zamunda."

686
01:19:24.014 --> 01:19:28.142
"Sire, Akeem and l
have depleted our funds."

687
01:19:28.351 --> 01:19:32.312
"Kindly send 300,000 American dollars
immediately,"

688
01:19:32.522 --> 01:19:36.900
"as we are in dire straits.
Your humble servant, Semmi."

689
01:19:37.110 --> 01:19:39.486
Semmi.

690
01:19:39.696 --> 01:19:44.450
- Should I make it 400,000?
- Do you think that'll be enough?

691
01:19:44.659 --> 01:19:47.327
You are right. 500,000.

692
01:19:48.204 --> 01:19:51.540
As long as you're asking,
why not go for a cool million?

693
01:19:51.750 --> 01:19:56.045
- Don't you think that's too much?
- Nah.

694
01:20:02.427 --> 01:20:05.012
Okay, what's going on?

695
01:20:05.221 --> 01:20:07.681
Patrice ... 

696
01:20:09.684 --> 01:20:11.977
I came to see Akeem.

697
01:20:12.187 --> 01:20:16.440
What are you involved in?
You can't afford this on your salary.

698
01:20:19.361 --> 01:20:23.822
Someone to kiss
Someone to miss

699
01:20:24.032 --> 01:20:28.035
When you're away
Through here, gone each day

700
01:20:28.244 --> 01:20:33.415
To be loved, to be loved
Wow! What a feeling

701
01:20:33.625 --> 01:20:38.962
- Quiet! People are trying to sleep.
- Some wish to be a king or a queen

702
01:20:39.172 --> 01:20:42.174
- Some wish for fortune and fame
- Shut up!

703
01:20:42.384 --> 01:20:47.262
But to be truly, truly, truly, truly loved

704
01:20:47.472 --> 01:20:51.141
it must mean all of these things

705
01:20:53.019 --> 01:20:57.064
Someone to care
Someone to share

706
01:20:57.273 --> 01:21:01.902
Lonely hours and moments of despair

707
01:21:02.112 --> 01:21:07.991
To be loved, to be loved
Wow! What a feeling

708
01:21:09.452 --> 01:21:12.746
Semmi, I just had the most wonderful ... 

709
01:21:14.207 --> 01:21:18.669
Hi, Akeem. Semmi told me everything.

710
01:21:20.005 --> 01:21:24.842
Sorry things didn't work out between
you and me, but you understand.

711
01:21:25.051 --> 01:21:28.679
Goodnight, sweet prince.

712
01:21:35.812 --> 01:21:38.772
Remember, you must not tell a soul

713
01:21:38.982 --> 01:21:44.194
Your secret is safe with me,
your Highness. Bye ... 

714
01:21:52.078 --> 01:21:55.122
If you're the prince, then who am l

715
01:21:58.168 --> 01:22:00.669
My servant.

716
01:22:12.932 --> 01:22:16.977
They smell good. Darryl must be
spending a fortune on flowers.

717
01:22:17.187 --> 01:22:19.855
Stay out of this, Dad.

718
01:22:20.065 --> 01:22:23.942
- Where are you going?
- To a museum. With Akeem.

719
01:22:24.152 --> 01:22:28.280
- I don't like that one bit.
- What's wrong with Akeem?

720
01:22:29.366 --> 01:22:32.326
You told me yourself.
He's a goat herder.

721
01:22:33.620 --> 01:22:38.624
Why don't you marry Darryl
He dresses nice, he treats you good.

722
01:22:38.833 --> 01:22:42.211
You only like Darryl because he's rich.

723
01:22:43.546 --> 01:22:47.841
I don't want you to have to struggle
like your mother and I did.

724
01:22:48.051 --> 01:22:51.470
I know. Bye, Daddy.

725
01:22:58.478 --> 01:23:00.688
Come in.

726
01:23:02.941 --> 01:23:07.736
- You boys wanted to see me.
- We would like to change apartments.

727
01:23:09.489 --> 01:23:12.282
Goddamn! What the hell
have you done in here?

728
01:23:12.492 --> 01:23:17.037
My friend Semmi has altered the
apartment, so we would like to change.

729
01:23:17.247 --> 01:23:18.914
This stuff ain't hot, is it?

730
01:23:19.124 --> 01:23:25.212
No, but I'm bringing a young lady up,
and she can't see me living like this.

731
01:23:26.840 --> 01:23:32.928
I'll let you boys stay in my apartment
and I'll move up here.

732
01:23:33.138 --> 01:23:38.475
- Does your apartment look poor?
- It's a real shithole. You'll love it.

733
01:23:39.769 --> 01:23:45.357
Here are the keys. It's apartment 1A.
Downstairs. First floor.

734
01:23:45.567 --> 01:23:49.403
Thank you, you're too kind.
Semmi, move our things.

735
01:23:57.454 --> 01:24:00.748
I have a date with Lisa.
Isn't that wonderful

736
01:25:19.619 --> 01:25:22.913
Who in the hell is that?

737
01:25:33.174 --> 01:25:39.304
What's up, brother? You're a little late
for the Christmas pageant.

738
01:25:43.268 --> 01:25:46.186
I'm King Jaffe Joffer, ruler of Zamunda.

739
01:25:46.396 --> 01:25:50.524
Have a seat. Chair number two
will be ready in a second.

740
01:25:53.862 --> 01:25:56.739
This is beautiful What is that - velvet?

741
01:25:58.908 --> 01:26:01.118
I have come for my son Akeem.

742
01:26:01.327 --> 01:26:06.165
- Who?
- You know, Kunta.

743
01:26:06.374 --> 01:26:12.588
- The boy upstairs.
- He live upstairs on the fifth floor.

744
01:26:15.008 --> 01:26:18.093
Who's going to clean up the flowers?

745
01:26:27.520 --> 01:26:30.147
You may enter.

746
01:26:36.946 --> 01:26:40.824
- You are not Akeem.
- I know that.

747
01:26:49.376 --> 01:26:52.753
- What is this?
- A photograph.

748
01:26:52.962 --> 01:26:55.047
What is this "McDowell's"?

749
01:26:55.256 --> 01:27:00.427
It's a place over on Queens Boulevard.
I think he works there.

750
01:27:00.637 --> 01:27:03.555
My son works?!

751
01:27:03.765 --> 01:27:09.353
- Where is he now?
- He moved to apartment 1A.

752
01:27:20.573 --> 01:27:23.992
Your Majesty.
What are you doing here?

753
01:27:24.202 --> 01:27:27.287
I received your telegram.
Where is Akeem?

754
01:27:28.707 --> 01:27:32.584
He went out. How was your flight?
Comfortable, I trust.

755
01:27:32.794 --> 01:27:37.756
Your job was to look after Akeem.
How could you let this happen?

756
01:27:37.966 --> 01:27:41.593
Akeem will not listen to me,
he's gone quite mad.

757
01:27:43.221 --> 01:27:45.055
Semmi ... 

758
01:27:45.265 --> 01:27:50.019
You've disgraced yourself,
and you must be punished.

759
01:27:50.979 --> 01:27:56.150
You will confine yourself to our
royal suite at the Waldorf-Astoria.

760
01:27:56.359 --> 01:28:01.488
See that he puts on some decent attire.
And bathe him thoroughly.

761
01:28:07.287 --> 01:28:09.705
Thank you, your Majesty!

762
01:28:11.833 --> 01:28:15.961
Look, Zamunda!
That's where you're from, isn't it?

763
01:28:16.171 --> 01:28:19.840
- What's it like?
- It's the most beautiful place on earth.

764
01:28:20.050 --> 01:28:26.347
The people are very friendly, and you ... 
You, they would treat like a queen.

765
01:28:31.978 --> 01:28:34.813
People will see us.

766
01:28:35.440 --> 01:28:38.150
Then let them see. Lisa ... 

767
01:28:38.360 --> 01:28:40.444
- Let us go.
- Now?

768
01:28:40.653 --> 01:28:43.489
Yes. Right now.

769
01:28:59.506 --> 01:29:05.302
Darryl, come by the house tonight.
About 9 p.m.

770
01:29:06.179 --> 01:29:08.806
Lisa will be home by then.

771
01:29:09.015 --> 01:29:12.309
Don't worry about it,
we'll work something out.

772
01:29:12.519 --> 01:29:15.104
Okay, see you later.

773
01:29:20.819 --> 01:29:25.197
There's some people here to see you.

774
01:29:26.991 --> 01:29:30.327
- Are they from McDonald's?
- I don't think so.

775
01:29:37.377 --> 01:29:40.004
What can I do for you?

776
01:29:43.049 --> 01:29:45.634
This is King Jaffe Joffer,
ruler of Zamunda.

777
01:29:45.844 --> 01:29:50.139
- He's searching for his son Akeem.
- Your son?

778
01:29:50.348 --> 01:29:54.393
- Yes, my son, the Prince.
- Prince? Are you serious?

779
01:29:54.602 --> 01:29:57.438
Prince Akeem is the sole heir
to the throne of Zamunda.

780
01:29:57.647 --> 01:30:00.774
I knew there was something special
about that boy.

781
01:30:00.984 --> 01:30:05.988
- Can you tell us where he might be?
- He's out with my lovely daughter Lisa.

782
01:30:08.533 --> 01:30:11.910
I'm staying at the Waldorf-Astoria.
When you see him, call me.

783
01:30:12.120 --> 01:30:14.371
- I'll tell him you're here.
- No.

784
01:30:14.581 --> 01:30:19.293
Do not alert him to my presence.
I shall deal with him myself.

785
01:30:25.175 --> 01:30:30.179
- For your trouble.
- Thank you, your RoyaIness.

786
01:30:40.690 --> 01:30:42.232
A prince!

787
01:31:04.589 --> 01:31:07.383
Wait! We cannot go in.

788
01:31:07.592 --> 01:31:09.510
Why not?

789
01:31:09.719 --> 01:31:12.805
Wait in the car. I will be right back.

790
01:31:22.941 --> 01:31:25.275
- We must leave.
- I don't care about the apartment.

791
01:31:25.485 --> 01:31:28.195
It's not that. I feel like I'm rushing you.

792
01:31:28.405 --> 01:31:30.489
No, you're not.

793
01:31:31.366 --> 01:31:35.035
- It's better if we take our time.
- But I want to.

794
01:31:35.245 --> 01:31:38.163
It's better if I take you home.

795
01:31:44.546 --> 01:31:49.383
Look who's here!
Akeem, it's good to see you.

796
01:31:49.592 --> 01:31:52.511
- It's good to see you, too.
- Have a drink.

797
01:31:52.721 --> 01:31:57.307
- I have to get going, Mr McDowell.
- You have time for one drink.

798
01:31:57.517 --> 01:31:59.184
Get out of here, dog.

799
01:31:59.394 --> 01:32:01.645
We don't spend enough time talking.

800
01:32:01.855 --> 01:32:04.440
Perhaps some other time,
I have to get going.

801
01:32:04.649 --> 01:32:08.193
Sit down,
I'll be right back with that drink.

802
01:32:25.712 --> 01:32:28.630
King Jaffe Joffer's room, please.

803
01:32:30.800 --> 01:32:33.719
Hello, King. Cleo McDowell here.

804
01:32:33.928 --> 01:32:37.097
Both the kids are here, together.

805
01:32:37.307 --> 01:32:43.062
2432 Derby Avenue,
Jamaica Estates. Right.

806
01:32:43.271 --> 01:32:46.982
King, I was wondering if ...  Hello, King?

807
01:32:50.612 --> 01:32:53.906
- I really have to go, sir.
- No. Have a seat right here.

808
01:32:54.115 --> 01:32:56.617
Did you want ice in that?

809
01:32:56.826 --> 01:32:59.244
Excuse me, I'll be right back.

810
01:33:10.840 --> 01:33:13.967
- Who was that?
- Jehovah's Witness.

811
01:33:15.387 --> 01:33:17.137
Excuse me.

812
01:33:23.395 --> 01:33:27.231
She doesn't like you anymore.
Get that through your greasy head!

813
01:33:27.440 --> 01:33:30.109
But you told me to come over.

814
01:33:32.821 --> 01:33:34.780
Now, where were we?

815
01:33:50.296 --> 01:33:53.007
I warned you, didn't l? Dottie, get him!

816
01:34:02.892 --> 01:34:05.811
I appreciate your hospitality,
but I have to get going.

817
01:34:06.021 --> 01:34:07.980
You can stay a little while longer.

818
01:34:08.189 --> 01:34:12.192
I just put some delicious hors d'oeuvres
in the oven ...  son.

819
01:34:13.278 --> 01:34:15.529
Let me go see if they're ready.

820
01:34:19.075 --> 01:34:22.119
- Lisa, I must leave.
- Is something wrong, Akeem?

821
01:34:23.204 --> 01:34:25.789
I'll tell you when the time is right,
but now I must go.

822
01:34:25.999 --> 01:34:29.001
Tell your father goodbye for me.

823
01:34:32.547 --> 01:34:34.840
- Where's Akeem?
- He had to leave.

824
01:34:35.050 --> 01:34:38.969
- He can't leave!
- What is going on?

825
01:34:39.179 --> 01:34:42.681
And why are you so nice to Akeem
all of a sudden?

826
01:34:42.891 --> 01:34:45.392
I like the boy.

827
01:34:45.602 --> 01:34:48.812
- What are you up to?
- What? Nothing.

828
01:34:49.022 --> 01:34:51.482
A man's got a right
to change his mind.

829
01:34:51.691 --> 01:34:56.028
- Daddy ... 
- You two make a beautiful couple.

830
01:34:56.237 --> 01:34:59.865
- Daddy ... 
- He's a real fine young man.

831
01:35:00.075 --> 01:35:06.205
- Dad!
- Okay, Lisa. He's rich. He is rich!

832
01:35:06.414 --> 01:35:09.041
- What?
- He's got his own money.

833
01:35:09.250 --> 01:35:15.047
When I tell you he's got his own money,
I mean the boy has got his own money.

834
01:35:22.430 --> 01:35:25.599
A prince. He's a prince!

835
01:35:28.103 --> 01:35:31.438
Lisa, you did it this time.
You hit the jackpot!

836
01:35:31.648 --> 01:35:35.484
Your goat herder makes Darryl
look like a welfare case.

837
01:35:49.207 --> 01:35:51.667
I will get out here.

838
01:35:52.752 --> 01:35:55.921
That'll be nine bucks.

839
01:36:17.944 --> 01:36:21.030
Good news, Akeem.
We've been rescued.

840
01:36:21.239 --> 01:36:26.201
- Where are my parents?
- They've gone to the McDowell's.

841
01:36:26.411 --> 01:36:28.537
- Come with me.
- Where are we going?

842
01:36:28.747 --> 01:36:30.664
Back to Queens.

843
01:36:32.042 --> 01:36:35.502
Look who's here! Come in, come in.

844
01:36:35.712 --> 01:36:38.505
Welcome to Casa de McDowell's.
Come right in.

845
01:36:48.516 --> 01:36:51.393
- Where is Akeem?
- He just stepped out.

846
01:36:51.603 --> 01:36:55.689
Probably went for a pizza.
You know these youngsters.

847
01:36:55.899 --> 01:36:59.610
This must be your lovely wife.
How are you today?

848
01:36:59.819 --> 01:37:01.779
Very well, thank you.

849
01:37:01.988 --> 01:37:06.784
I don't know whether to shake
your hand, kiss it or bow or what.

850
01:37:06.993 --> 01:37:10.204
I feel like break dancing.

851
01:37:10.413 --> 01:37:16.251
Come in, have a seat, take a load off.
Your son ought to be back in a minute.

852
01:37:16.461 --> 01:37:20.172
- Try the Lazy-Boy. It's comfortable.
- It's very nice.

853
01:37:20.382 --> 01:37:22.174
Put your feet up.

854
01:37:29.849 --> 01:37:32.559
Here you go, King.
Try one of these pigs in a blanket.

855
01:37:32.769 --> 01:37:34.978
They're the frozen kind,
but you'd never know it.

856
01:37:35.188 --> 01:37:38.023
You told me my son was here.

857
01:37:38.233 --> 01:37:42.861
My daughter Lisa might know where
he went. They've gotten quite close.

858
01:37:43.071 --> 01:37:46.031
Where is your daughter?
I must speak to her at once.

859
01:37:46.616 --> 01:37:49.451
Lisa?
There's someone here to see you.

860
01:37:55.667 --> 01:37:59.086
This is Akeem's father. The King!

861
01:37:59.295 --> 01:38:01.338
Leave us.

862
01:38:10.390 --> 01:38:14.059
- I understand you're seeing my son.
- I was seeing him.

863
01:38:14.269 --> 01:38:16.311
So you know about his wife
in Zamunda?

864
01:38:16.521 --> 01:38:18.981
- He's married?
- No, but he will be soon.

865
01:38:19.190 --> 01:38:23.110
We've already chosen his bride.
So you see ... 

866
01:38:23.319 --> 01:38:25.863
 ... he cannot be serious about you.

867
01:38:26.072 --> 01:38:30.367
Akeem came to America to ... 
sow his royal oats.

868
01:38:31.828 --> 01:38:34.246
Excuse me, I need to be alone.

869
01:38:34.456 --> 01:38:38.792
Are you comfortable, Miss ... 
I'm not sure what to call you.

870
01:38:39.002 --> 01:38:44.173
- My name is Cleo.
- Nice to meet you. My name's Aoleon.

871
01:38:44.382 --> 01:38:47.051
Aoleon. Aeolon ... 

872
01:38:50.555 --> 01:38:55.893
Lisa, where are you going?
I want you to meet the Queen.

873
01:38:56.102 --> 01:39:02.107
- Are you all right, my dear?
- I'm sorry. I have to get out of here.

874
01:39:02.317 --> 01:39:04.943
What's the matter, baby?

875
01:39:10.158 --> 01:39:12.326
What did you say to my daughter?

876
01:39:12.535 --> 01:39:16.246
The truth. That Akeem
could not be interested in her.

877
01:39:16.456 --> 01:39:21.418
- How can you be so sure?
- Our son can't consort with such a girl

878
01:39:21.628 --> 01:39:24.129
Now, wait a minute!

879
01:39:25.340 --> 01:39:26.757
Oha ... 

880
01:39:30.095 --> 01:39:34.181
You have been inconvenienced,
and I'm prepared to compensate you.

881
01:39:34.391 --> 01:39:37.643
- Shall we say 1 million dollars?
- No way.

882
01:39:37.852 --> 01:39:41.313
- 2 million.
- You can't buy my daughter off.

883
01:39:41.523 --> 01:39:45.067
- Nonsense!
- Jaffe, apologise to Mr McDowell.

884
01:39:45.276 --> 01:39:48.821
I will not. The man is beneath me,
and so is his daughter.

885
01:39:49.030 --> 01:39:52.449
I don't give a damn who you are.
This is America, Jack.

886
01:39:52.659 --> 01:39:57.746
You say one more word about Lisa,
and I'll break my foot off in your ass.

887
01:39:59.124 --> 01:40:02.835
- Pardon me?
- What's everybody yelling about?

888
01:40:03.044 --> 01:40:07.089
Their son, the Prince, loves your sister,
but the King can't handle it.

889
01:40:07.298 --> 01:40:10.718
No, he's not.
The Prince is in love with me.

890
01:40:16.141 --> 01:40:19.309
- Are you all right?
- Yes, Mother. I'm fine.

891
01:40:19.519 --> 01:40:22.521
Why are you hugging him?
He's just the servant.

892
01:40:23.857 --> 01:40:27.192
He's the Prince.

893
01:40:28.611 --> 01:40:31.155
Who told you that?

894
01:40:37.495 --> 01:40:41.540
- You mean Akeem's the Prince?
- Yeah, and he's in love with Lisa.

895
01:40:41.750 --> 01:40:44.918
How come she always gets
the good ones?

896
01:40:47.797 --> 01:40:51.633
- Where is Lisa?
- Your daddy ran her off.

897
01:40:55.680 --> 01:40:58.682
- What did you tell her?
- It is of no consequence.

898
01:40:58.892 --> 01:41:03.354
- We shall return to Zamunda at once.
- I will not leave without Lisa.

899
01:41:03.563 --> 01:41:06.440
So you do care for her?

900
01:41:08.109 --> 01:41:11.070
Mother, I love her.

901
01:41:11.279 --> 01:41:13.906
Then go after her.

902
01:41:18.536 --> 01:41:23.540
- Akeem! I forbid you.
- Put a sock in it, Jaffe. The boy's in love.

903
01:41:49.984 --> 01:41:52.444
Darryl, what happened?

904
01:41:54.322 --> 01:41:58.951
- Lisa dumped me.
- I know. You poor thing.

905
01:42:00.995 --> 01:42:06.417
The first thing we have to do
is get you out of these wet clothes.

906
01:42:08.795 --> 01:42:10.754
Stop!

907
01:42:10.964 --> 01:42:14.675
Lisa!

908
01:42:19.973 --> 01:42:22.224
I will be fine by myself.

909
01:43:13.068 --> 01:43:15.277
Lisa, please.

910
01:43:16.196 --> 01:43:19.281
I did not mean to hurt you.

911
01:43:19.491 --> 01:43:23.327
Well, at least I know
who gave me these.

912
01:43:23.536 --> 01:43:27.081
You can keep them,
'cause I don't want them ... 

913
01:43:27.290 --> 01:43:29.917
 ... and I don't want you.

914
01:43:46.685 --> 01:43:48.268
Just leave me alone!

915
01:43:48.478 --> 01:43:51.647
Lisa, please. I love you.

916
01:43:51.856 --> 01:43:54.191
What about the woman
you are supposed to marry?

917
01:43:54.401 --> 01:43:57.319
I don't love her.
Why do you think I came here?

918
01:43:57.529 --> 01:44:00.572
Your father told me -
to sow your royal oats.

919
01:44:00.782 --> 01:44:06.328
I came to America to find my bride.
I came to Queens to find you.

920
01:44:06.538 --> 01:44:10.708
So why did you lie to me? Why didn'
you just tell me you were a prince?

921
01:44:10.917 --> 01:44:14.378
I wanted you to love me for who I am.

922
01:44:14.587 --> 01:44:18.507
- I'm not sure who are.
- I'm the man you fell in love with.

923
01:44:18.717 --> 01:44:21.552
Should it matter that I am a prince?

924
01:44:24.472 --> 01:44:25.806
It shouldn', but l ... 

925
01:44:26.016 --> 01:44:31.478
Say you never loved me,
and I won't bother you again.

926
01:44:38.653 --> 01:44:41.947
It just wouldn't work out,
we're too different.

927
01:44:42.157 --> 01:44:44.616
You're royalty, for God's sake.

928
01:44:44.826 --> 01:44:46.785
Do you want me
to renounce my throne? I will.

929
01:44:46.995 --> 01:44:51.331
I renounce my throne. I am no longer
the Prince of Zamunda.

930
01:44:51.541 --> 01:44:53.792
I renounce my throne!

931
01:44:58.256 --> 01:45:01.133
Does this make you happy?

932
01:45:09.976 --> 01:45:13.395
I can't let you do that.

933
01:45:13.605 --> 01:45:16.482
I do not care about my crown.

934
01:45:16.691 --> 01:45:19.693
All I care about is you.

935
01:45:19.903 --> 01:45:22.529
Marry me, Lisa.

936
01:45:27.077 --> 01:45:32.623
- So, what do you think?
- Go on, honey. Take a chance.

937
01:45:45.637 --> 01:45:50.683
Look, I'm sorry. I can'.
Goodbye, Akeem.

938
01:45:58.066 --> 01:46:01.735
If you're really a prince, I'll marry you.

939
01:47:18.605 --> 01:47:23.650
Look at it this way. At least we learned
how to make French fries.

940
01:47:50.095 --> 01:47:53.055
You're still not speaking to me.

941
01:47:54.099 --> 01:47:57.476
- I only want our son to be happy.
- And so do l.

942
01:47:57.686 --> 01:48:01.146
Aoleon, please. It is out of our hands.
The girl told him no.

943
01:48:01.356 --> 01:48:04.608
After the way you treated her,
who could blame her?

944
01:48:04.818 --> 01:48:09.113
Even if she said yes, they still couldn'
marry. It's against the tradition.

945
01:48:09.322 --> 01:48:11.949
Well, it is a stupid tradition.

946
01:48:12.701 --> 01:48:16.995
- Who am I to change it?
- I thought you were the King.

947
01:49:40.747 --> 01:49:46.043
Your Highness.
We have not come to that part yet.

948
01:49:53.677 --> 01:49:57.721
Your Highness. Your Highness!

949
01:50:25.625 --> 01:50:28.127
Would you really
have given this up for me?

950
01:50:28.336 --> 01:50:31.839
Of course. If you like,
we can give it all up now.

951
01:50:34.884 --> 01:50:36.468
Nah!

952
01:51:45.372 --> 01:51:48.332
Wait a minute, wait a minute!
Stop right there.

953
01:51:48.541 --> 01:51:51.126
Listen! Stop right there a minute.

954
01:51:51.336 --> 01:51:54.171
A man goes in to a restaurant.
Are you listening?

955
01:51:54.381 --> 01:51:58.884
A man goes into a restaurant.
He sits down and has a bowl of soup.

956
01:51:59.094 --> 01:52:01.804
He says to the waiter,
"Come, taste the soup".

957
01:52:02.013 --> 01:52:04.848
The waiter says, "Is there something
wrong with the soup?" "Taste the soup."

958
01:52:05.058 --> 01:52:08.102
"Is the soup too hot?"
"Will you taste the soup?"

959
01:52:08.311 --> 01:52:11.188
"Is the soup too cold?"
"Will you just taste the soup!"

960
01:52:11.398 --> 01:52:14.525
"All right, I'll taste the soup.
Where's the spoon?"

961
01:52:21.700 --> 01:52:24.410
What do you know from funny,
you bastard?
